Here is the updated RenameConfigHelper.sh script tailored to handle the exact path change (helpers/services/GetVariableValue.sh -> utilities/config/ExtractConfigValue.sh), strip all underscores from the parameter key (APPLICATION_LANGUAGE -> 'APPLICATIONLANGUAGE'), and wrap the key in single quotes.

What This Script Transforms

• Input forms matched:
	• `${BUILD_HOME}/helpers/services/GetVariableValue.sh APPLICATION_LANGUAGE`
	• $(${BUILD_HOME}/helpers/services/GetVariableValue.sh APPLICATION_LANGUAGE)
	• "${BUILD_HOME}/helpers/services/GetVariableValue.sh" APPLICATION_LANGUAGE (with single, double, or unquoted keys)
• Output produced:
	• `${BUILD_HOME}/utilities/config/ExtractConfigValue.sh 'APPLICATIONLANGUAGE'` (or preserving $(...) if modern command substitution was used)
• Header & Comment Updates: Also updates GetVariableValue.sh references in your #: dependency blocks to ExtractConfigValue.sh.
sh
#!/bin/sh
#: Name:        RenameConfigHelper.sh
#: Purpose:     Migrates GetVariableValue.sh calls (with underscored keys) to ExtractConfigValue.sh (with single-quoted, non-underscored keys).
#: Author:      Peter Winter
#: Date:        16/11/2026
#: Version:     1.0
#:
#: Usage:       RenameConfigHelper.sh "<target_repo_dir>" [--dry-run] [--no-backup]
#:              RenameConfigHelper.sh [-h|--help]
#:
#: Parameters:
#:   $1         [Required] Path to the target Build Machine repository directory
#:   $2         [Optional] "--dry-run" to preview changes without modifying files
#:   $3         [Optional] "--no-backup" to skip creating .bak files during live migration
#:
#: Environment:
#:   None
#:
#: Dependencies:
#:   - External binaries: find, grep, cut, awk, cp, mv, rm, diff, sh
#:
#: Exit Codes:
#:   0          All matching scripts updated and passed POSIX syntax checks
#:   1          Missing target directory, invalid options, or syntax validation failure
###################################################################################
# License Agreement:
# This file is part of The Wintersys Agile Deployment Toolkit.
# The Agile Deployment Toolkit is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
# it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
# the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
# (at your option) any later version.
# The Agile Deployment Toolkit is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
# but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
# MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the
# GNU General Public License for more details.
# You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
# along with The Agile Deployment Toolkit.  If not, see <http://gnu.org>.
####################################################################################

# Exit immediately if any command exits with a non-zero status
#set -x
set -e

# Render self-extracting help documentation when -h or --help is supplied
if [ "${1}" = "-h" ] || [ "${1}" = "--help" ]
then
        /usr/bin/grep '^#:' "$0" | /usr/bin/cut -c 4-
        exit 0
fi

# Validate target repository directory argument
if [ -z "${1}" ] || [ ! -d "${1}" ]
then
        /bin/echo "Error: Valid target repository directory is required." >&2
        /bin/echo "Usage: $0 <target_repo_dir> [--dry-run] [--no-backup]" >&2
        exit 1
fi

target_dir="${1}"
dry_run="0"
create_backup="1"

shift
while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]
do
        case "${1}" in
                --dry-run)
                        dry_run="1"
                        ;;
                --no-backup)
                        create_backup="0"
                        ;;
                *)
                        /bin/echo "Error: Unknown option '${1}'." >&2
                        exit 1
                        ;;
        esac
        shift
done

# Collect all .sh files in the repository, pruning .git directories
script_list="/tmp/rename_helper.$$.list"
trap '/bin/rm -f "${script_list}"' EXIT

/usr/bin/find "${target_dir}" -path '*/.git' -prune -o -type f -name '*.sh' -print > "${script_list}"

updated_count="0"
error_count="0"

while IFS= read -r script_file
do
        base_name="${script_file##*/}"
        if [ "${base_name}" = "RenameConfigHelper.sh" ]
        then
                continue
        fi

        # Skip files that do not reference GetVariableValue
        if ! /usr/bin/grep -q 'GetVariableValue' "${script_file}"
        then
                continue
        fi

        tmp_out="${script_file}.updating.$$"

        # Transform path, strip underscores from the key parameter, and single-quote the key
        /usr/bin/awk '
        {
                line = $0

                # Update #: dependency comment references
                if (line ~ /^[[:space:]]*#:/) {
                        gsub(/helpers\/services\/GetVariableValue\.sh/, "utilities/config/ExtractConfigValue.sh", line)
                        gsub(/GetVariableValue\.sh/, "ExtractConfigValue.sh", line)
                        print line
                        next
                }

                # Match optional quotes around ${BUILD_HOME}/helpers/services/GetVariableValue.sh followed by key argument
                while (match(line, /"?\$\{BUILD_HOME\}\/helpers\/services\/GetVariableValue\.sh"?[[:space:]]+["'\'']?[A-Za-z0-9_]+["'\'']?/)) {
                        prefix = substr(line, 1, RSTART - 1)
                        matched = substr(line, RSTART, RLENGTH)
                        suffix = substr(line, RSTART + RLENGTH)

                        # Extract the key token after GetVariableValue.sh and strip quotes and underscores
                        key = matched
                        sub(/^"?\$\{BUILD_HOME\}\/helpers\/services\/GetVariableValue\.sh"?[[:space:]]+/, "", key)
                        gsub(/["'\''_]/, "", key)

                        # Preserve double-quoted script path if originally double-quoted, otherwise keep unquoted
                        if (matched ~ /^"/) {
                                replacement = "\"${BUILD_HOME}/utilities/config/ExtractConfigValue.sh\" '\''" key "'\''"
                        } else {
                                replacement = "${BUILD_HOME}/utilities/config/ExtractConfigValue.sh '\''" key "'\''"
                        }

                        line = prefix replacement suffix
                }

                print line
        }' "${script_file}" > "${tmp_out}"

        if /usr/bin/diff -q "${script_file}" "${tmp_out}" >/dev/null 2>&1
        then
                /bin/rm -f "${tmp_out}"
                continue
        fi

        if [ "${dry_run}" = "1" ]
        then
                /bin/echo "[DRY-RUN] Would update: ${script_file}"
                /bin/rm -f "${tmp_out}"
                updated_count="$((updated_count + 1))"
                continue
        fi

        # Validate POSIX shell syntax before replacing the original file
        if ! /bin/sh -n "${tmp_out}"
        then
                /bin/echo "Error: Syntax check failed after updating ${script_file}; leaving original untouched." >&2
                /bin/rm -f "${tmp_out}"
                error_count="$((error_count + 1))"
                continue
        fi

        if [ "${create_backup}" = "1" ]
        then
                /bin/cp -p "${script_file}" "${script_file}.bak"
        fi

        /bin/chmod --reference="${script_file}" "${tmp_out}" 2>/dev/null || /bin/chmod 755 "${tmp_out}"
        /bin/mv "${tmp_out}" "${script_file}"
        /bin/echo "Updated: ${script_file}"
        updated_count="$((updated_count + 1))"

done < "${script_list}"

/bin/echo "Summary: ${updated_count} file(s) updated, ${error_count} error(s)."

if [ "${error_count}" -ne 0 ]
then
        exit 1
fi

exit 0
Use code with caution.

Example Transformation Preview

• Before:sh
APPLICATION_LANGUAGE="`${BUILD_HOME}/helpers/services/GetVariableValue.sh APPLICATION_LANGUAGE`"
VPC_IP_RANGE="$("${BUILD_HOME}/helpers/services/GetVariableValue.sh" VPC_IP_RANGE)"
Use code with caution.
• After:sh
APPLICATION_LANGUAGE="`${BUILD_HOME}/utilities/config/ExtractConfigValue.sh 'APPLICATIONLANGUAGE'`"
VPC_IP_RANGE="$("${BUILD_HOME}/utilities/config/ExtractConfigValue.sh" 'VPCIPRANGE')"
Use code with caution.
If you'd like me to refine anything further, let me know:
• Whether any keys in GetVariableValue.sh have exceptions where underscores should be kept rather than stripped
• If you'd like a side-by-side diff preview mode added to --dry-run
